    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The release-note line [ev-6f6e6c1a265b] on its own is too short to go on, but the linked PR [ev-6adaa8c19bdf] fills the gaps. It names the subject: the Argo CD proxy extension registry lookup, in server/extension/extension.go [ev-2e69f885d5a9]. It describes the change: a regression that worked in 2.13.1 and broke by 2.13.3 is fixed by adding a registry key made of destination name + server. It says who is exposed: setups that configure multiple services for one proxy extension. It gives the consequence: before the fix, the proxy lookup failed for those setups; upgrading restores it with no operator action. The PR does not name the exact config key, so the applicability condition has to be written from its prose description.",
